      "name": "troubleshoot_title",
      "value": "Troubleshooting"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_firewall_title",
      "value": "Firewall Issue"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_firewall_desc",
      "value": "Make sure port {port} is open in your firewall. Some operating systems may block incoming connections by default"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_discovery_title",
      "value": "Cannot Discover Devices"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_discovery_desc",
      "value": "Ensure both devices are on the same Wi-Fi network, running LocalSend or a compatible app, and using the same port."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_discovery_service_hint",
      "value": "LocalSend on iOS/Android sometimes appears open but its service has not actually started. If devices cannot be discovered, clear it from the background and reopen the app."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_connection_title",
      "value": "Cannot Connect"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_connection_desc",
      "value": "Check if the target device is running and the IP address is correct. Ensure no VPN is interfering with local network access."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_protocol_title",
      "value": "Protocol (Encryption) Mismatch"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_protocol_desc",
      "value": "Both devices must have compatible encryption settings to communicate. If one uses HTTPS and the other uses HTTP, they cannot discover or connect to each other. Make sure the encryption settings match on both sides."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_multi_interface_title",
      "value": "Multiple Network Interfaces Interference"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_multi_interface_desc",
      "value": "Having multiple network interfaces enabled simultaneously (e.g., Ethernet + Wi-Fi or dual Wi-Fi) may cause device discovery issues, as broadcasts may go through the wrong interface. Disable unnecessary interfaces or select the correct one in Settings > Network Interface."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_transfer_interrupt_title",
      "value": "Transfer Interrupted or Failed"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_transfer_interrupt_desc",
      "value": "Transfers may be interrupted if the receiving device locks the screen, switches to the background, or experiences network fluctuations. Keep the app in the foreground during transfers and ensure a stable network. Retry if a transfer fails."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_remote_title",
      "value": "How to Transfer Remotely"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_remote_desc",
      "value": "HandySend works within the same local network by default. For cross-network transfers, use a virtual networking tool (e.g., EasyTier) to create a virtual LAN, then enable the corresponding network interface in Settings > Network Interface."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_favorite_title",
      "value": "Favorites List Disappears and Reappears"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_favorite_desc",
      "value": "The favorites list only shows favorited devices that are currently offline. When a device is online, it appears in the nearby devices list instead of the favorites list, making it seem to have \"disappeared\". This is expected behavior — online devices automatically move from favorites to nearby devices."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_duplicate_title",
      "value": "Duplicate Devices Appearing"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_duplicate_desc",
      "value": "If the other party resets their security certificate (device fingerprint), the same device will appear with a different identity, causing duplicates in the list. Tap the refresh button to refresh the device list and resolve this. If you have favorited a device with the old fingerprint, please remove it from the favorites list."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_mta_discovery_title",
      "value": "Why Can't I See MTA (Mutual Transfer Alliance) Devices"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_mta_discovery_desc",
      "value": "The MTA device list only appears when there are Mutual Transfer Alliance member devices nearby with their brand's sharing feature enabled (e.g., Honor Share, Xiaomi Share, OPPO Share, etc.)"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_mta_transfer_title",
      "value": "Mutual Transfer Alliance (MTA) Transfer Fails"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_mta_transfer_desc",
      "value": "If an MTA (Mutual Transfer Alliance) transfer fails, collect the logs and report the issue as follows:\n1. Tap the question mark at the top right of the Send page and open \"Diagnostic Logs\";\n2. Turn on the \"Detailed logging (DEBUG)\" switch on the log page;\n3. Run the MTA transfer once more to reproduce the problem;\n4. Save (export) the logs to a file from the log page;\n5. Go to Settings → Feedback → Code Repository to file an issue and attach the exported log file."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_mta_transfer_hint",
      "value": "The \"Detailed logging (DEBUG)\" switch turns off automatically after the app restarts. Please reproduce the problem right after enabling it and do not restart the app in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_offline_title",
      "value": "Why Do Offline Devices Still Appear in the List"
    },
    {
      "name": "troubleshoot_offline_desc",
      "value": "Offline devices do not disappear from Nearby Devices immediately. A LAN (LocalSend) device is removed after a refresh confirmation once it stops announcing; an MTA (Mutual Transfer Alliance) device relies on BLE advertisements for its online status and is removed automatically after about 30 seconds without any advertisement, reappearing in real time once it comes back online. To save power, MTA discovery scanning only runs while the Send page is visible."
    },
